### PLM API walkthrough: open in IntelliJ IDEA (HTTP Client) or VS Code (REST Client extension).
### Start the stack first: `make up` then `make run`. Run the requests top to bottom.
### X-PLM-User picks who you are. It is TEMPORARY until Keycloak login (roadmap 0.8).

@api = http://localhost:8080/api/v1
@partType = 00000000-0000-7000-8000-000000000102

### 1. The site (root) context
# @name site
GET {{api}}/contexts/site

### 2. Create an organization
# @name org
POST {{api}}/contexts
Content-Type: application/json

{ "parentId": "{{site.response.body.id}}", "kind": "ORGANIZATION", "name": "Acme {{$random.uuid}}" }

### 3. Create a product inside it
# @name product
POST {{api}}/contexts
Content-Type: application/json

{ "parentId": "{{org.response.body.id}}", "kind": "PRODUCT", "name": "Drone X1" }

### 4. List types (Document, Part and any subtypes)
GET {{api}}/types

### 5. Create a part -> A.1
# @name part
POST {{api}}/objects
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "typeId": "{{partType}}",
  "contextId": "{{product.response.body.id}}",
  "name": "Motor mount",
  "attributes": { "material": "AL6061", "massKg": 0.12 }
}

### 6. Check out as alice -> working copy A.2
POST {{api}}/objects/{{part.response.body.id}}/checkout
X-PLM-User: alice

### 7. Bob tries too -> 409 ALREADY_CHECKED_OUT
POST {{api}}/objects/{{part.response.body.id}}/checkout
X-PLM-User: bob

### 8. Edit the working copy
PATCH {{api}}/objects/{{part.response.body.id}}/working-copy
X-PLM-User: alice
Content-Type: application/json

{ "attributes": { "material": "Ti-6Al-4V", "massKg": 0.09 } }

### 9. Check in -> A.2 becomes the latest, immutable iteration
POST {{api}}/objects/{{part.response.body.id}}/checkin
X-PLM-User: alice
Content-Type: application/json

{ "comment": "Switch to titanium" }

### 10. Revise -> B.1
POST {{api}}/objects/{{part.response.body.id}}/revise

### 11. History, newest first: B.1, A.2, A.1
GET {{api}}/objects/{{part.response.body.id}}/iterations
